<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	Deliberately empty beyond this comment, for now — kept as a real file
	(not omitted) because App Store Connect / Xcode signing wants an
	entitlements file to attach capabilities to as they're added later.

	App Intents / App Shortcuts (Intents/JarvisIntents.swift) need NO
	entitlement here — unlike the legacy SiriKit Intents framework (which
	needed a "Siri" capability + an Intents Extension target), the modern
	App Intents framework (iOS 16+) exposes shortcuts directly from the
	main app target with no extra entitlement or extension. This is a real
	API-shape difference from older "SiriKit Intents" patterns, confirmed
	against Apple's own current App Intents documentation before writing
	this file — not a corner cut.

	Keychain access (Identity/KeychainStore.swift) also needs no entry
	here: `kSecAttrAccessibleAfterFirstUnlockThisDeviceOnly` with no
	`kSecAttrAccessGroup` uses this app's own default, implicit keychain
	access group (derived from its bundle identifier / app ID prefix by
	the OS), which every app gets for free — an explicit
	"keychain-access-groups" entitlement is only needed to SHARE a keychain
	item across multiple apps/extensions, which this app doesn't do.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
